01. COPYRIGHT AND OWNERSHIP

Copyright © 2026 [FULL LEGAL NAME OR REGISTERED ENTITY].

All rights reserved, subject to applicable law, third-party rights, and permissions expressly granted by the relevant rights holder.

MedOrbits is an education, admissions, career guidance, recruitment, and application-services project. This license establishes the intended terms governing access to and use of original materials in which the identified rights holder owns or controls the relevant intellectual property rights.

The rights holder reserves all rights in those materials that are not expressly granted through a valid license, written authorization, applicable agreement, or operation of law.

1.1 Ownership principles

Ownership must be established by evidence, not by branding or repository presence alone.

The following, individually or collectively, do not necessarily establish ownership of every project component:

* The MedOrbits name or brand identity.
* Registration or control of a website domain.
* Ownership or administration of a source-code repository.
* Publication of a copyright notice.
* Creation of a website, application, or technical document.
* Payment for development services without an applicable ownership agreement.
* Possession, downloading, hosting, or distribution of project materials.

The relevant ownership analysis may require authorship records, employment or contractor agreements, assignments, licenses, contributor permissions, and third-party license terms.

1.2 No automatic transfer

No transfer of copyright or other intellectual property ownership occurs merely because a person accesses, views, downloads, clones, hosts, stores, or otherwise receives project materials.

Ownership and permitted use remain subject to the actual rights held by the relevant party, applicable agreements, and applicable law.

1.3 Reservation of ownership claims

Nothing in this document authorizes the rights holder to claim ownership of works owned by another person or entity.

Where ownership is shared, disputed, licensed, assigned, or otherwise limited, this license applies only to the extent that the relevant rights holder is legally entitled to grant the applicable permissions.

