02. DEFINITIONS

For purposes of this license:

2.1 Project means MedOrbits and its associated websites, applications, repository materials, documentation, and related resources, to the extent applicable.

2.2 Rights holder means the individual or legal entity that owns or is legally authorized to license the relevant rights in a particular work.

2.3 Covered materials means original copyrightable materials owned or controlled by the rights holder and falling within the scope of Section 03.

2.4 Recipient means any individual, organization, company, institution, developer, contractor, or other party accessing or receiving covered materials.

2.5 Third-party materials means software, content, data, media, trademarks, documentation, or other works owned, supplied, or licensed by parties other than the relevant rights holder.

2.6 Written authorization means a valid permission, license, or agreement issued by a person or entity authorized to grant the relevant rights.

2.7 Proprietary software means software components for which the relevant rights holder retains proprietary rights and has not granted a broader license, subject to third-party rights and applicable law.

2.8 Derivative work means a work that legally qualifies as a derivative of a protected work under applicable law. Whether a particular modification, adaptation, or combination qualifies depends on the relevant facts and law.

2.9 Commercial use means use for commercial advantage or monetary compensation, to the extent the term is relevant under an applicable authorization or agreement.

2.10 Applicable law means the laws, regulations, and binding legal requirements that apply to the relevant materials, parties, conduct, and circumstances.

These definitions clarify the intended scope of the license. They do not expand ownership or create rights that the rights holder does not possess.

