03. SCOPE OF COVERED MATERIALS

Subject to Section 04, this license applies to original MedOrbits materials only to the extent that the rights holder owns or controls the relevant rights.

3.1 Software and source code

Covered materials may include:

* Original HTML, CSS, JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, and other source code.
* Original frontend interfaces, backend services, application modules, and utilities.
* Original API implementations, application logic, and integration code.
* Original database schemas, migrations, scripts, and data-processing implementations.
* Original build, validation, deployment, and maintenance scripts.
* Original configuration templates and technical implementations.
* Original code comments, implementation documentation, and software-specific manuals.
* Original automated testing utilities and proprietary development tools.

Third-party packages, libraries, frameworks, and externally licensed code remain subject to their respective licenses.

3.2 Website design and creative works

Covered materials may include:

* Original page layouts and graphic compositions.
* Original interface components, styling, and visual treatments.
* Original illustrations, artwork, graphics, and promotional materials.
* Original logos, icons, and brand artwork, where the relevant rights are owned.
* Original written copy, descriptions, and creative website materials.
* Original animations, visual compositions, and interface presentation assets.
* Original combinations and arrangements of creative elements, to the extent legally protected.

The presence of externally sourced images, fonts, icons, or other creative assets does not make those assets proprietary to MedOrbits.

3.3 Educational and informational content

Covered materials may include:

* Original educational guides and explanatory materials.
* Original admissions and application-preparation guides.
* Original career guidance and recruitment documentation.
* Original articles, manuals, reference materials, and informational publications.
* Original explanatory summaries and editorial analyses.
* Original instructional resources and learning materials.
* Original compilations, taxonomies, and curated datasets, to the extent legally protected.

Facts, ideas, methods, procedures, and official information are not automatically protected merely because they appear in an original document.

3.4 Structured data and documentation

Covered materials may include:

* Original JSON datasets and data structures.
* Original schemas, validation rules, and data-model definitions.
* Original README files, engineering specifications, and architecture documents.
* Original support, security, operational, and maintenance documentation.
* Original project templates, manuals, and technical documents.
* Original arrangements and compilations of information, where legally protected.
* Original data-processing and transformation implementations.

Individual data elements, factual information, third-party records, and external source materials remain subject to their applicable legal status and permissions.

3.5 Future and additional materials

Other original copyrightable works may fall within this license when incorporated into or distributed as part of the Project and when the rights holder owns or controls the relevant rights.

Inclusion in a repository, website, application, archive, or deployment package is not, by itself, proof of ownership.

