The fact that information is publicly accessible does not necessarily mean that every form of reproduction or commercial reuse is permitted.

4.4 Trademarks and third-party branding

Third-party names, logos, service marks, trademarks, and brand assets remain the property of their respective owners.

Their appearance within the Project does not imply ownership, sponsorship, endorsement, partnership, or affiliation.

4.5 User-submitted and contributor materials

Content submitted by applicants, users, institutions, agencies, employees, contractors, or external contributors is not automatically transferred to the rights holder through submission, storage, publication, or repository inclusion.

Ownership and permitted use depend on applicable rights, agreements, permissions, and law.

4.6 Unprotected material and legal exceptions

