Except for rights expressly granted through a separate valid authorization, rights provided by applicable third-party licenses, and uses permitted by applicable law, this document does not grant permission to reproduce, modify, adapt, publish, distribute, sublicense, or commercially exploit covered materials.

5.1 Written permissions

The rights holder may authorize particular uses through a written license, signed agreement, approved contributor arrangement, or other legally valid permission.

The person granting permission must possess authority to grant the relevant rights.

5.2 Recommended authorization terms

Where appropriate, an authorization should specify:

1. The exact works or materials covered.
2. The authorized individual, organization, or recipient class.
3. The permitted purposes and activities.
4. Whether copying, modification, adaptation, or redistribution is allowed.
5. Whether commercial use is permitted.
6. Attribution and copyright-notice requirements.
7. Any applicable fees, duration, territory, or sublicensing conditions.
8. Restrictions on transfer or further licensing.
9. Termination conditions and any continuing obligations.
10. Applicable dispute-resolution and governing-law terms, where legally appropriate.

5.3 Component-specific permissions

A permission concerning one file, module, dataset, or creative work does not automatically extend to the entire Project.

An authorization should be interpreted according to its actual wording, the rights held by the grantor, and applicable law.

5.4 No implied authorization

Silence, technical access, repository visibility, or the absence of a license file in an individual subdirectory does not automatically establish permission to reuse proprietary materials.

Where the applicable rights are unclear, obtain clarification from the verified rights holder before undertaking restricted use.

