06. RESTRICTIONS ON UNAUTHORIZED USE

To the extent permitted by applicable law and subject to valid permissions and third-party rights, recipients must not undertake the following activities without the necessary authorization.

6.1 Unauthorized reproduction

Reproduce or republish protected proprietary source code, documentation, original creative works, or protected compilations without authorization.

6.2 Unauthorized redistribution

Distribute or publish substantial portions of covered materials through another repository, website, package, template marketplace, application, or distribution service without the necessary rights.

6.3 Unauthorized modification and derivative works

Modify, adapt, translate, or distribute derivative works based on protected materials without authorization, except where permitted by applicable law.

6.4 Commercial exploitation

Sell, sublicense, rent, repackage, or commercially exploit covered materials without an applicable license or other legal permission.

6.5 Product or template repurposing

Repackage proprietary website templates, original design assets, application modules, or protected content as another product or service without authorization.

6.6 False claims of ownership

Misrepresent authorship, ownership, endorsement, affiliation, or authorization concerning works owned by the rights holder.

6.7 Improper removal of notices

Remove, falsify, or misrepresent copyright and license notices where doing so infringes relevant rights or violates applicable law or license conditions.

6.8 Misuse of branding

Use MedOrbits branding, logos, or protected brand assets in a manner that falsely implies authorization, endorsement, ownership, or affiliation.

6.9 Circumvention of access restrictions

Circumvent technical access controls or use credentials without authorization where such conduct violates applicable law, valid agreements, or the rights governing the relevant system.

6.10 Unauthorized extraction or republication of protected compilations

Extract, reproduce, or republish protected compilations or database arrangements where the relevant conduct infringes rights actually held by the rights holder or violates applicable contractual or statutory restrictions.

Nothing in this section prohibits conduct authorized by the rights holder or expressly permitted by applicable law.

